    "summary": "Root cause: the instance layer carried girder.count_per_span = 4, contradicting the description's \"3 girders per span\". At model-check time the L2-1 recomputation of girder.A/I (rule MR-02, A_single·I_single × n_girders) used n_girders = 4, yielding A = 4.556 m² and I = 1.420 m⁴, which disagreed with the accepted decisions (3.417 m², 1.065 m⁴) and with girder.w/girder.m derived from them — giving the 4 empty-suspect L2-1 failures.\n\nFix: corrected the instance (write_instance) with girder.count_per_span = 3 as stated in the description, then re-proposed girder.A, girder.I, girder.w and girder.m (evidence MR-02 / MR-07 + instance inputs) so their values and provenance were re-established. The instance now recovers A_single = 1.1389 m², I_single = 0.35492 m⁴ from the small-box section, giving girder.A = 3.4168 m², girder.I = 1.06475 m⁴, w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m — all in agreement.\n\nModel (spine_beam_2d, simply_supported, 30 m span): 3 precast prestressed small-box girders C40, γ=26 kN/m³, Ec=32500 MPa; plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers, Ge=1 MPa) at both abutments, 6 per line (2 per girder end × 3 girders), Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, rotation free.\n\nResults: f1 = 3.402 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN each (sum 2665.1 kN = 88.836 × 30, matching w·L); self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m; lane (Class II, 2 lanes, ξ=1.0, qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk=240 kN, μ=0.201) max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m. All L1/L2/L3 checks pass."
